5. Vocabulary-card kanji panel

The kanji panel on vocabulary cards shows a dictionary-style reading and
meaning (훈음) for each kanji and, where available, a 모양 line naming the
kanji's first-level parts. These fields are selected from the following
sources; a part name not found there comes from the project's own reviewed
table.

When a learner imports the kanji addon built from their own Gilbut PDFs,
the panel shows that addon's 훈음 instead for every kanji and part it
covers. Those values are extracted on the learner's computer and are not
distributed in this repository, the core APKG, or the builder.

  * libhangul data/hanja/hanja.txt (commit
    a34aef73378c0992316861bbf13fc914ee7577d9), Copyright (c) 2005,2006
    Choe Hwanjin, BSD 3-Clause license. The license text is in
    licenses/libhangul-hanja-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
  * KanjiVG (commit 422b5538595676da918c288a4230cb5e22a1ee7e),
    (c) Ulrich Apel, Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). Only the first-level
    components of each kanji are copied: https://kanjivg.tagaini.net/
    Those KanjiVG-derived 모양 values are distributed under the same license.
  * BabelStone IDS (IDS.TXT, file date 2025-06-27) by Andrew West:
    https://babelstone.co.uk/CJK/IDS.TXT. Its header waives rights in the
    data; attribution is given voluntarily.
  * CJK Decomposition Data (cjk-decomp, commit
    c29b391fd6267e7a3541387e03a3dd60b1cd34d1) by Aaron Madlon-Kay, used under
    the Apache License 2.0 (licenses/cjk-decomp-Apache-2.0.txt). Nine
